      "duration": 54.96,
      "text": "Hello everyone, my name is Gisela Beyerano, and I am a system professor at Marys University in New York. I'm going to talk today to you about my work in sign language processing for accessibility. I would like you to think for a while how is COVID-pandemic for all of us? Remember how those times were so difficult for all of us? Now, I would like you to imagine how difficult those times could have been for communities such as the Deaf Communities. Not all the TV shows or sources of information would provide interpreters to guarantee the access to information on this key topic to Deaf Communities. There are 700 millions of Deaf people around the world, according to the word Federation of the Deaf.",
