      "start": 56.61,
      "end": 125.53,
      "duration": 68.92,
      "text": "And some of them, of course, or most of them, have sign languages as their first language or native language. That means that some of them may not know the oral language in their country. In fact, there are 300 more or less sign language in the world. There is no unique sign language for all the Deaf Communities in different countries. So, that's why lip-reading or captioning may not always be the best way to go to assist and support the communication of these communities. Not also the gloves that have been a technology that was provided as helpful. When in reality, they would focus more on the movement of hands. Sign languages imply not only movement of hands, shapes, or other characteristics, but facial gestures and pose two of the body.",
